# Record field missing: under BAS width subtyping, accessing a field not in the
# annotation's known fields returns Unknown (not an error). The annotation @[x: Int]
# constrains the parameter to have at least field x, but does not rule out field y —
# BAS allows extra fields via width subtyping. No warning is emitted.
# Eval proceeds — the function is defined but never called.
[f: [fn [let r@[x: Int]] r.y]]
=== out
["f": [fn [let r] ...]]
